hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1673","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Aziz al-Ayli, that Salama narrated to them, from Uqayl, that Muhammad ibn Muslim informed me, that Mahmud ibn Rabi' al-Ansari informed him, that Itban ibn Malik said to him: Then when the sun had risen high at midday, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and Abu Bakr (RA) came. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) asked for permission to enter, so I granted him permission. He did not sit down until he entered the house, then he said: \Where would you like me to pray in your home?\"" Itban said: So I gestured to him toward a corner of the house. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood"," pronounced the takbir"," so we stood"," lined up in rows"," and he prayed two voluntary rak'ahs"," then he concluded the prayer with the salam."""
